PMAlarm/
# The unanchored PMAlarm/ rule above is correct for the 18 runtime alarm-data
# directories it was written for (the repo root plus one inside every
# HT9011UC_Code_*/HT9046LS_Code_* version tree), but it also matched three of
# the V906 .dfm-conversion pipeline's GENERATED CANONICAL trees, because golden
# has a form named PMAlarm*.dfm and the generators mirror golden's relative
# paths. Effect: git tracked only 130 of 133 forms, so tools/dfm2rc's G7
# fidelity/idempotency gates could not pass from a fresh clone or worktree --
# regeneration produced 3 "extra" forms (PMAlarmInterFace, PMAlarmShowData,
# fMain) and 801 G7_EXTRA_IN_REGEN diffs. Un-ignoring the three trees
# run_b1d.py treats as canonical (IR_OUT_CANON / RC_OUT_CANON /
# LAYOUT_OUT_CANON, run_b1d.py:78-80) rather than weakening the rule itself.
# res_out/ stays ignored: it holds rc.exe .res build output, never tracked.
!HT9011UC_Cpp_V3.33.906.0/tools/dfm2rc/ir_out/PMAlarm/
!HT9011UC_Cpp_V3.33.906.0/tools/dfm2rc/rc_out/PMAlarm/
!HT9011UC_Cpp_V3.33.906.0/tools/dfm2rc/layout_out/PMAlarm/
# AI(W906-PT-W2) 20260807: the same unanchored-rule collision, third occurrence --
# this time on the V906 PORT SOURCE directory. Translation wave PT-W2 landed
# PMAlarm/PMAlarmSystem.{cpp,h} and PMAlarm/uTimeTool.{cpp,h}; `git add` refused
# them and would have committed a CMakeLists.txt referencing sources that are not
# in the repo -- i.e. a tree that builds here and nowhere else. Same remedy as the
# three lines above: un-ignore the specific path rather than weaken a rule that is
# correct for the 18 runtime alarm-data directories it was written for.
!HT9011UC_Cpp_V3.33.906.0/PMAlarm/
dmc_data/
SECS/GPM/
MDB/
dclusr50/
hklib/
EXE/
elec/
document/
Initial/
SICON/
Tool/
ABS-3372/
BVL-3766/

# --- Large binary/image/ini directories ---
# AI(W906-FW0) 20260817: anchored to root -- the unanchored form also swallowed web/assets/img/ (web HMI assets)
/IMG/
bmp/
IniData/
system/
HT9011UC_Cpp_V3.33.906.0/build_last.log
